# The header dependencies of every object, as the compiler saw them.
#
# The rules above name each object's source and, at most, the one header of the
# same name. A header included from anywhere else - parameter.hpp, logger.hpp,
# qunibusdevice.hpp, device_configuration.hpp, and every register or bit
# definition a device carries - reaches nearly every object and is named by
# almost none of them, so editing one used to leave the objects that include it
# stale and link them into the binary unchanged.
#
# -MMD writes each object's real include list to a .d file beside it, which is
# read back here; -MP adds a phony target per header so deleting one does not
# break the build with "no rule to make target". The first build of a clean tree
# has no .d files and the explicit rules cover it; every build after that has
# the full list.
-include $(OBJECTS:.o=.d) $(OBJDIR)/main_demo.d $(OBJDIR)/main_qbone_web.d
